# Copy to .env.local for local dev (gitignored), or set in Netlify's
# Site settings -> Environment variables for production builds.

# FormSubmit (https://formsubmit.co) endpoint for the contact form, which
# posts to https://formsubmit.co/<this value>. One-time activation:
#   1. Set this to the inbox email address (e.g. contacttempoacademy@gmail.com),
#      deploy, and submit the form once.
#   2. FormSubmit emails that inbox an activation link. Click it.
#   3. FormSubmit then shows (and emails) a random-string ID for the form.
#      Replace the email address here with that ID and redeploy, so the
#      address isn't exposed in the page source.
# Until this is set, the contact form on /contact is disabled and shows an
# email fallback instead of posting to a dead endpoint.
VITE_FORMSUBMIT_ID=
